[[Image:Ife still.gif|right|Still spell]]
[[Image:Gui_still.png|right|Stilled indicator]]
{{feat
|type=metamagic
|prereq=ability to cast first-level spells
|reqfor=[[automatic still spell]]
|desc=Still spells are cast without a somatic [[component]]. Any [[spell failure|penalties]] incurred from casting in armor do not apply to a spell prepared with this feat.
|use=A stilled spell occupies a [[spell slot]] one level higher than normal.
|bonus1=wizard
}}

==Notes==
* The spells that can be stilled are those that have a somatic component. In addition, ''[[knock]]'' can be stilled even though it does not have a somatic component. That leaves the following spells that cannot be used with this feat. (This list excludes level 9 spells, as those cannot be stilled due to the lack of spell slots above level 9.)
**[[Blindness/deafness]]
**[[Darkness (spell)|Darkness]]
**[[Displacement]]
**[[Flare]]
**[[Light]]
**[[Mass charm]]
**[[Polymorph self]]
**[[Power word, stun]]
**[[True strike]]

==Builder notes==
'''Item feat:''' No, But it can be added with custom content.

==Custom content notes==
'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' yes

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*This feat can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] and works as an item feat, but [[wizard]]s and [[divine]] spellcasters will only need to have the item equipped while preparing their [[spellbook]]s, not while [[rest]]ing or casting. [[Spellhook]]ing can be used to verify that the caster has the [[feat]] if it is used as an item feat.